.TH "SYSTEM-SUITE" "1" "Sep 2026" "system-suite 1.3.1" "System Suite Manual"

.SH NAME
.PP
system-suite \- Terminal-based system maintenance, monitoring, and optimization toolkit

.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBsystem-suite\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
\fBsystem-suite\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBsystem-suite\fR is a unified, terminal-based system monitoring and maintenance toolkit
designed for macOS, Linux, and Unix-like environments. It provides interactive dashboards,
smart disk cleanup, multi-platform package updates, network speed testing, service management,
and interactive file discovery.

When executed without arguments in an interactive terminal, \fBsystem-suite\fR launches an interactive
menu. When invoked with a subcommand or in non-interactive environments, it executes the specified command
directly and cleanly terminates.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinfo\fR
Display complete system metrics, CPU utilization, memory breakdown, storage targets, and network details.
.TP
\fBcleanup\fR [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Inspect and clean safe temporary files, caches, application logs, and development artifacts.
\fB\-\-dry-run\fR previews targets without deletion. \fB\-\-yes\fR confirms execution in batch mode.
.TP
\fBupdate\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Check and perform package upgrades across active system package managers (Homebrew, APT, DNF, Pacman, Zypper, PKG, etc.).
.TP
\fBbackup\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Create compressed archives (.tar.gz) of configured directories with automatic timestamping and cataloging.
.TP
\fBmonitor\fR
Display running processes sorted by resource consumption (supports htop if available).
.TP
\fBspeed\fR
Run network speed and latency benchmarks using the best native tool available (\fBnetworkQuality\fR on macOS, \fBspeedtest-cli\fR, or \fBcurl\fR fallbacks).
.TP
\fBservice\fR
List, inspect, and manage system background services (supports systemctl on Linux and launchctl on macOS).
.TP
\fBbattery\fR
Show battery health metrics, charge cycles, and power diagnostics (macOS and Linux upower).
.TP
\fBlogs\fR
View and filter System Suite audit and operational logs.
.TP
\fBfind\fR
Interactive fuzzy finder for files, recently modified items, or file types (supports fzf).
.TP
\fBtime\fR
Display date, time, calendar, and system uptime.
.TP
\fBcompletion\fR \fIbash|zsh\fR
Generate shell autocompletion script for the specified shell.
.TP
\fBman\fR [\fIDIR\fR]
View the manual page or export \fBsystem-suite.1\fR to \fIDIR\fR.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Assume yes and bypass confirmation prompts for non-interactive modifications (e.g. cleanup, update, backup).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry-run\fR
Preview actions (specifically cleanup) without modifying or deleting files.
.TP
\fB\-\-non-interactive\fR, \fB\-\-no-interactive\fR
Force non-interactive batch mode execution.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print concise usage instructions and available options.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the current version of \fBsystem-suite\fR.

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
\fBSYSTEM_SUITE_DISK_PATH\fR
Specify the primary mount point or directory path used for disk capacity metrics and alerts (default: \fB$HOME\fR).
.TP
\fBBACKUP_SOURCES\fR
Space-delimited list of directories to include during backup generation.
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
If set, suppresses ANSI color formatting for plain text output and pipeline integration.

.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.config/system_suite/\fR
Directory containing user configuration files.
.TP
\fB~/.local/share/system_suite/\fR
Data storage directory containing operational logs and cached metadata.
.TP
\fB~/.local/share/system_suite/backups/\fR
Default destination for created backup archives.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Launch interactive menu dashboard:
.RS
.nf
$ system-suite
.fi
.RS

.PP
Display system information overview:
.RS
.nf
$ system-suite info
.fi
.RE

.PP
Preview disk cleanup targets safely:
.RS
.nf
$ system-suite cleanup --dry-run
.fi
.RE

.PP
Run non-interactive package updates in cron or automation:
.RS
.nf
$ system-suite update --yes
.fi
.RE

.PP
Install Zsh shell completion:
.RS
.nf
$ system-suite completion zsh > ~/.zsh/completions/_system-suite
.fi
.RE

